== rules ==
#tort 

Easy.
Paper is cut by scissors.
Scissors cut the paper.
Scissors are broken by rock.
Like dinosaurs.
But rock hates paper...
Never understood why...
But maybe all I needed was paper at the time...
Anyway, do you want to play now?

* Alright, let's play!
-> rockpaperscissors
* I'm sorry, I'd rather not.
-> norps

== rockpaperscissors ==
 #tort

VAR choice = ""
LIST options = (Rock),(Paper),(Scissor)
VAR result = ""

Okay so, close your eyes and make a choice.
 + [Rock]
    ~ choice = "Rock"
 + [Paper]
    ~ choice = "Paper"
 + [Scissor]
    ~ choice = "Scissor"

- You chose {choice} 
~ result = LIST_RANDOM(options)
and Tortilla chose {result}.
{
    - choice == "Rock" && result == Scissor:
        Oh, well played, you beat me! Very lucky!
    - choice == "Rock" && result == Paper:
        Oopsie I'm sorry, I guess I won this time!
    - choice == "Scissor" && result == Rock:
        Oopsie I'm sorry, I guess I won this time!
    - choice == "Scissor" && result == Paper:
        Oh, well played, you beat me! Very lucky!
    - choice == "Paper" && result == Rock:
        Oh, well played, you beat me! Very lucky!
    - choice == "Paper" && result == Scissor:
        Oopsie I'm sorry, I guess I won this time!
    - else:
        Hihi, I guess we both got lucky then hehe. We both lost... Or we both won!
}

* You're a nice rock paper scissors player for sure. #score #good
- Thank you, I appreciate.
...
I guess I had time to train, lol.
Anyway, it's getting late.
But I'm happy I got to know you better.
You are kind. And you too are lucky.
Our fate lie in the stars.
It's about the place and about the time.
And I'm sure someday, somewhere, you will figure it all out.
Take good care my friend!
* I appreciate Tortilla, thank you so much. Have a nice evening.

-> ending

